      "message": "Soften the raw-Bitcoin-address privacy notice in Send dialog\n\nThe on-chain privacy callout was destructive-red, required ticking a\ncheckbox before the Send button enabled, and forced a two-tap confirm\nregardless of amount. That was overkill for an informational warning\nabout an inherent Bitcoin property — sending to a bc1 address isn't\nitself dangerous.\n\nDrop the checkbox + acknowledgement state, stop using raw-address as a\ntrigger for the two-tap arm (large amounts still arm), and restyle the\nAlert as a soft amber notice with the same Learn-more popover.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "cad509093f8cebeafe5f234193fee63408220674",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/cad509093f8cebeafe5f234193fee63408220674"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/commits/2238f94edeb3ee54289efa5a994a58695ec5b9ef",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEESof9JJzQIzN3kpf4chHR+ZdE+7cFAmoUwxAACgkQchHR+ZdE\n+7fZkRAAwNRzUz8mJhvgVNiYopERuviOgr5wt/N8gRK6sOzhuLc4Um9H9M9gCCWq\nnKaY0sdZGap+hSyFQW6636fuJ+TCedCHFVeRl+jz1qCIz4qAcHxiKXwdDrw5aPcx\nMxjIgd5zuNx71jabTa2SMW1MsbAakoZ7qQrGPyMGRV38Es3kN18sgJCycDFOXHP5\nkVaIW3R2MrH3hVkXDZBJIav3f3CDPGiXs6ltluLhDoxMvVFdkiZ3OmbilZI8CxKh\nD/Fu2bm3TR/AEMMR9/YshNTa2PRqo3rr2UpvFsu7mke+6Xs14pKTA53nDyd8mPjh\nLkaGsdNiURLk4yla7u2STPaKfVoPWILyityrQv20Ia8+cMAhm8bNRvW0N7HM3bRo\nBp8Emy5sj+4hdXbYfLtjuxtoSkwUoh3DZ68vidsdqX98x5WLwAXo2gdtcZYWc0oh\nYGLVJEElTr9+HsAnnkJjSa5FsI2XyZiHNeLFVVrp/nqQYsyEbUDXkcMT7RFS5LuG\nO6haComwZDI7ymMhUSJ/CC5Zc8rRnDbpUHMwFqrSiB61EmLuLIv/avtmA0g7F2IX\nL+Mn30bhKkGlSBBSzwmbk/RumqN8aNKZKp+rIj005l0vhFyWATJ8GjqwdGOmv4sn\nEdw8USRBD4IYBhtSC7kb2QtnTcNk/rZUg1ajGrQqyi4kar7KNSU=\n=63Ni\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree cad509093f8cebeafe5f234193fee63408220674\nparent f9248da8147bce3292f9583c4726a65a78745765\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1779745552 -0500\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1779745552 -0500\n\nSoften the raw-Bitcoin-address privacy notice in Send dialog\n\nThe on-chain privacy callout was destructive-red, required ticking a\ncheckbox before the Send button enabled, and forced a two-tap confirm\nregardless of amount. That was overkill for an informational warning\nabout an inherent Bitcoin property — sending to a bc1 address isn't\nitself dangerous.\n\nDrop the checkbox + acknowledgement state, stop using raw-address as a\ntrigger for the two-tap arm (large amounts still arm), and restyle the\nAlert as a soft amber notice with the same Learn-more popover.\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-05-25T22:47:40Z"
      }
