      "message": "Surface both sp and bc1 rows when a BIP-21 URI carries both\n\nA BIP-21 URI like `bitcoin:bc1q…?sp=sp1q…` advertises a silent-payment\nrecipient with an on-chain fallback. The dropdown collapsed this to the\nsp row only, hiding the fallback path even though the sender might\nprefer the (cheaper, simpler) on-chain leg.\n\nSplit the URI into independent `btcCandidate` and `spCandidate` strings\nand show whichever rows are valid. Sp goes first so the privacy-\npreferred option is selected by default, matching the QR scanner's\nprioritization.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "c6b3018c907b1bab8fe2f67b3461bbb66877c274",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/c6b3018c907b1bab8fe2f67b3461bbb66877c274"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/commits/f9248da8147bce3292f9583c4726a65a78745765",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEESof9JJzQIzN3kpf4chHR+ZdE+7cFAmoUwiAACgkQchHR+ZdE\n+7dl+A//WPoB7EOnn0Tyyc3Tbjq4SvEkImT1f5NNrLuvWrqqedmm8F1QRrf01K1G\nH3N5D5v80q3xG46otbFTaDi8cmKYwD8mIpDtcn4Hb03ncUhRmH80pfACjCt8pnnQ\n7q3yrvJLsaF8l25U/O0YPeAhHk+4Vt5Qvm+H9x/ENuDWeaD78xLUN39/LY+EkJBj\n4dnnlpegQ0OsEXWfuJ3Ujif16k+ev/0N8KJXUApx1j8YGtQ7b1f6GkPSTh3gNo5i\n5a+kI1DnOiqGYbxaMNN8Nlnn/+kjK3hwmGeahjaGOXfiRPcQYEEAPcW1Nv2Cs9dR\n8HXhrXTmXe7sO5f4zU1nrDVN084JzOeTC7bzpLUIWxMtEMH//g19UHbjcBPK5jwI\naiqNUyuc8xaCZ0xTU/mGwdisLab35udlUh4tvzIJJ8ZCuR+Uvh4LowNeBr+8T+gf\naosApCiUXIVtRcTFKm4YnJnl4lcAYoGeQWB+33XhQm8rDJGW71mRBfhtz4zhyioJ\n/tbZl6PuuJ37GCKdwiVS0DzfojHw5PDRpGwQt18UakoAEtzUvMx+qltAUIJbQuZh\nRyD5i4GVMLKkUC/O76dqRmLfZ4JGpRvgIjb7sOo/CVMYltswduDAweN7ll8IixU7\nVKulYHdDh1ajiu7pX5gmaNxL078NSCC4JVfBX6iUmV4GncEMDhs=\n=+akQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree c6b3018c907b1bab8fe2f67b3461bbb66877c274\nparent 0b248d48dfd7a548ae463860ddeb8e64856994cb\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1779745312 -0500\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1779745312 -0500\n\nSurface both sp and bc1 rows when a BIP-21 URI carries both\n\nA BIP-21 URI like `bitcoin:bc1q…?sp=sp1q…` advertises a silent-payment\nrecipient with an on-chain fallback. The dropdown collapsed this to the\nsp row only, hiding the fallback path even though the sender might\nprefer the (cheaper, simpler) on-chain leg.\n\nSplit the URI into independent `btcCandidate` and `spCandidate` strings\nand show whichever rows are valid. Sp goes first so the privacy-\npreferred option is selected by default, matching the QR scanner's\nprioritization.\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-05-25T22:47:40Z"
      }
