        "payload": "tree f143a85ed341e28e61f763f15dcaa69577f8ab6c\nparent 5227508257536d203c8c0e692ebc0d42bf6b94ca\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1779745138 -0500\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1779745138 -0500\n\nSuppress profile search when wallet recipient is an address or BIP-21 URI\n\nWhen a bitcoin: URI was pasted into the Send dialog, the parsed sp1…\nrecipient row appeared for a frame, then got buried under stale NIP-50\nsearch results matching parts of the URI string. Raw bc1/sp1 addresses\nwere mostly spared only because the relay's NIP-50 search rarely matches\nrandom bech32 strings.\n\nSkip useSearchProfiles entirely (and drop any prior results) once the\ntrimmed input parses as a valid Bitcoin address, silent payment address,\nor bitcoin: URI. Also avoids leaking the recipient address to the search\nrelay.\n\nRegression-of: 52275082\n",
