      "message": "Accept BIP-21 URIs pasted into the wallet Send recipient field\n\nThe Send Bitcoin dialog's QR scanner already parses bitcoin:<addr>?sp=…\nURIs, but pasting the same URI into the input field fell through to the\nplain on-chain validator and was rejected.\n\nExtract the BIP-21 parsing into parseBitcoinUri() and reuse it from both\nthe scanner and the input-time recipient detection, so paste matches the\nscan behaviour: prefer a valid sp= silent payment, otherwise fall back\nto the on-chain address.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "892cb45fabe191b84ef6e458691e1e6c0137b6e0",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/892cb45fabe191b84ef6e458691e1e6c0137b6e0"
